odus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.13-005024","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In the article we look at relational processes of engagement, negotiation and articulation of digital heritage knowledge production. By looking at creative reuse and remix of digital cultural heritage we focus on how those processes manifest at the intersection of established cultural institutions and people outside of these institutions. Two experimental arrangements are described that seek to understand how Human-Computer Interaction and design interventions might contribute to new forms of heritage knowledge production and collective memory-making by mobilizing infrastructuring interventions to question knowledge production, politics and ownership. We conclude by proposing that HCI can contribute to infrastructuring for collective knowledge production by supporting arrangements that open access to digital cultural heritage, open heritage knowledge and its practices, and reimagine authorship and ownership of contributions to heritage.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Marttila, Sanna-Maria","Botero, Andrea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381774"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Collective Memory making","Digital cultural heritage","Human Computer Interaction","Infrastructuring","Knowledge production"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructuring for collective heritage knowledge production","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-77431-8_6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381774","ids":["itu-21bf76dc-d39d-4faa-b9fe-5e5bc652adbd"],"keyword":["Collective Memory-making","Digital Cultural Heritage","Human-Computer Interaction","Infrastructuring","Knowledge Production"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E3A8B55F5A57578ADFC739B373F255F4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-77431-8_6","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"boteropau","last":"Botero","name":"Botero, Andrea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Part of the Lecture Notes in Computer Science book series (LNCS, volume 12795)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-21bf76dc-d39d-4faa-b9fe-5e5bc652adbd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructuring for Collective Heritage Knowledge Production","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381774","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This workshop explores the relevance of the notion of commons as an objective, and commoning as a way of doing and being for design. We invite the PD community to reflect on ways in which these concepts help us critically protect and support sustainable futures for communities of humans and non-humans. How can participatory design remain open to multiple ways of sharing and different worldviews? What would it mean for the participatory design community in terms of challenging established notions such as participation, facilitation, empowerment, to name but a few? How can participatory design contribute further to theoretical elaboration and activist practices?","author_count":7,"contributors":["Botero, Andrea","Marttila, Sanna-Maria","Poderi, Giacomo","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Seravalli, Anna","Teli, Maurizio","Van Amstel, Frederick M. C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384610"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","title":"Participatory Design Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Federal University of Technology - Paraná","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Collaborative design","Commoning","Commons","commons design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"commoning design and designing commons","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85173278/PDC_Workshop_CommoningDesign_SHARE_V.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384610","identifier":[{"id":"85087389197","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e2f5bc2e-9b56-40bb-bd30-66e335790ed9"],"keyword":["Collaborative Design","commoning","commons","commons design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-7F3BA82A6D3B529ED71439D00E8B142E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85173278/PDC_Workshop_CommoningDesign_SHARE_V.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"br","key":"federal university of technology paraná","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Federal University of Technology - Paraná","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"boteropau","last":"Botero","name":"Botero, Andrea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giacomo","key":"poderipau","last":"Poderi","name":"Poderi, Giacomo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"seravallipau","last":"Seravalli","name":"Seravalli, Anna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"telipau","last":"Teli","name":"Teli, Maurizio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederick M. C.","key":"vanamstelpau","last":"Van Amstel","name":"Van Amstel, Frederick M. C.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3384772.3385162","eisbn":["9781450376068"],"pages":"178-180","place":"New York, NY, US","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"(PDC ’20: Vol. 2), June 15–20, 2020, Manizales, Colombia","title":"PDC '20: Proceedings of the 16th Participatory Design Conference 2020 - Participation(s) Otherwise - Volume 2","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087389197"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e2f5bc2e-9b56-40bb-bd30-66e335790ed9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Commoning Design and Designing Commons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384610","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This e-zine documents the discussions and group work done at the ‘Infrastructuring in Participatory Design’ workshop, a full-day event that took place at the Participatory Design Conference 2018 in Hasselt and Genk, Belgium¹. The workshop invited the Participatory Design (PD) community to come together, with their cases or projects, questions and topics of interest in order to take stock of empirical insights and conceptual developments around the notions of infrastructure and infrastructuring, and their relevance to the revitalization of the political agenda of PD. Following a hands-on approach, participants - collectively and critically - mapped issues, disentangled assumptions, identified blind spots, and outlined new research opportunities charting the possibilities and limitations of an infrastructuring approach in Participatory Design at large. Participants at the workshop came from a broad range of domains (e.g. Design, Science and Technology Studies, Anthropology, Social Sciences, Information Sciences, Architecture), representing interests in infrastructuring from multiple perspectives. Prior to the workshop, participants were asked to 1) write a position statement and read everyone else's position statements, 2) look at their own work in relation to the theme of the workshop to pick one artifact to bring to the workshop, 3) contribute to a collective compilation of research literature dealing with infrastructures and infrastructuring. With these activities, we together prepared issues, ideas, and concerns to work with in the workshop.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Botero, Andrea","Karasti, Helena","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Geirbro, Hanne Cecilie","Baker, Karen","Parmiggiani, Elena","Marttila, Sanna-Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381734"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","University of Oulu"],"keyword":["Infrastructuring","Participatory Design","e zine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drawing together infrastructuring and politics for participatory design a visual collection of cases issues questions and relevant literature","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jultika.oulu.fi/files/isbn9789526222042.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381734","ids":["itu-1f91d4a7-816c-454a-bfa4-b35fe1657fe9"],"keyword":["Participatory design","e-zine","infrastructuring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-28A9B39654EDD6EF1C7025625888BE35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://jultika.oulu.fi/files/isbn9789526222042.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/handle/2142/103012","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of oulu","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oulu","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Co-Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"boteropau","last":"Botero","name":"